UID:yom-kippur-20271011@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271012
SUMMARY:Yom Kippur
DESCRIPTION:Yom Kippur\, the Day of Atonement\, falls on the tenth day of T
 ishri\, nine days after Rosh Hashanah\, and begins at sunset the evening b
 efore the date a civil calendar shows. It is the most widely kept fast in 
 Judaism and the one day of the year on which the high priest of the Jerusa
 lem Temple was permitted to enter the Holy of Holies. What the Torah actua
 lly commands is not a fast: it says to practice self-denial\, and the spec
 ifics are the rabbis' work.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/yom-kip
 pur/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/yom-kippur/
CATEGORIES:Community
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
